# ==============================================================================
# Business Helper: Production & Local Environment Variables Template
# Copy this file to .env.local for local development, or set these variables in
# your cloud platform environment settings (Vercel, Netlify, Railway).
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Supabase Backend Infrastructure (Database, Auth & Storage)
# Required for multi-tenant database access, RLS policies, and SPEI receipts
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.your-anon-key
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.your-service-role-key

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. SAT CFDI 4.0 PAC Invoicing (Facturapi.io)
#
# Two independent settings:
#
#   FACTURAPI_SECRET_KEY is the *platform's* PAC account fallback — DEPRECATED
#   by the BYOK decision (2026-08-12, docs/STATUS.md §05): the platform never
#   stamps on behalf of tenants, so leave this UNSET in every deployment. Each
#   organization connects its own PAC in Ajustes; without one,
#   /api/invoices/issue refuses with a clear message rather than recording a
#   stamp that never happened. The code path remains only until its removal
#   lands (tracked on the tracker).
#
#   PAC_ENCRYPTION_KEY seals the API keys tenants connect (AES-256-GCM). 32
#   bytes, base64 or hex — generate with:
#       node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
#   Rotating it makes every stored key unreadable; tenants must reconnect.
#   Business Helper never stores CSD certificates (.cer/.key) — those stay with
#   the user's PAC. See docs/02-architecture/cfdi_integration_architecture.md.
#
# Sandbox Key format: sk_test_... | Production Key format: sk_live_...
# A sk_test_ key stamps against the PAC sandbox: valid-looking documents with no
# fiscal validity. Issuance refuses to use one in production.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FACTURAPI_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_your_facturapi_secret_key
PAC_ENCRYPTION_KEY=base64_32_byte_key_for_sealing_tenant_pac_keys

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Stripe Subscription Billing ($299 / $599 / $999 MXN)
# Required for SaaS billing checkout sessions and webhook entitlement listener.
# Without STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, /api/stripe/checkout answers 503 — it creates a real
# Checkout Session and has no placeholder URL to fall back to. The tier is
# granted only by the webhook, so STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET is required to make a
# completed payment take effect.
#
# Each STRIPE_PRICE_* is the id of a Price object you create in *your* Stripe
# account — copy it from the dashboard; it is not derivable and there is no
# default. A tier whose variable is unset cannot be sold: checkout answers
# 503 STRIPE_PRICE_NOT_CONFIGURED and names the variable in the server log.
#
# It must be the **Price** id (price_…), not the **Product** id (prod_…). The
# dashboard shows the product id at the top of the product page and the price id
# further down, under Pricing; taking the wrong one is what took live checkout
# down on 2026-08-11. Checkout answers a product id with "No such price", so the
# route now refuses it up front with 503 STRIPE_PRICE_MISCONFIGURED and names
# the variable and the value in the server log.
# The values below are shaped like real ids on purpose; they belong to no
# account and will 404 at Stripe if left as they are.
#
# Verify the map before charging anyone — `npm run verify:stripe` reads the
# account and every price back from Stripe and fails if a tier bills an amount
# the pricing page does not advertise. It is read-only and safe against live.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_your_stripe_secret_key
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_your_stripe_webhook_signing_secret
# STRIPE_PRICE_INICIAL is the current name; STRIPE_PRICE_EMPRENDEDOR still works.
STRIPE_PRICE_INICIAL=price_replace_with_your_inicial_299mxn_price_id
STRIPE_PRICE_EMPRENDEDOR=price_replace_with_your_inicial_299mxn_price_id
STRIPE_PRICE_NEGOCIO=price_replace_with_your_negocio_599mxn_price_id
STRIPE_PRICE_EMPRESA=price_replace_with_your_empresa_999mxn_price_id
# Folio packs are one-time prices, not subscriptions. Unset until #24/#27 ship
# a purchase route — nothing reads them today.
# STRIPE_PRICE_FOLIO_50=
# STRIPE_PRICE_FOLIO_200=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. E-signature OTP (email via Resend) + Outbound WhatsApp (Twilio / Meta)
#
# OTP_SECRET keys the OTP digests and the digital seals on signed quotes. The
# app throws in production when it is unset. Generate with:
#     openssl rand -hex 32
# Rotating it invalidates outstanding codes and makes stored seals
# unverifiable against a recomputation — treat it as long-lived.
#
# OTP_DELIVERY_CHANNEL selects how a signer receives their code. Leave it unset
# only in development, where codes go to the server console; in production an
# unset channel fails closed and the signing flow answers 502, because echoing
# the code back over HTTP would hand every signature to whoever asked for one.
#
#   email    -> Resend API: needs RESEND_API_KEY and OTP_EMAIL_FROM
#   sms      -> DEPRECATED. Twilio Messages API: SID, AUTH_TOKEN, TWILIO_SMS_NUMBER
#   whatsapp -> DEPRECATED. Twilio when TWILIO_WHATSAPP_NUMBER is set, else Meta
#
# email is the launch channel (founder decision, 2026-08-11): one API key and a
# verified sending domain, no WABA, no carrier registration. The signer's code
# goes to clients.email, so a client without one cannot be sent a code — the
# route answers 422 naming the missing field. sms/whatsapp still work for a
# deployment already configured with them, but are deprecated and log a warning
# per send. Phone-number *login* stays retired — an email or phone here is
# where a code is delivered, never a credential.
#
# Verify the channel before trusting it — the check calls the provider and,
# with OTP_TEST_EMAIL (or OTP_TEST_PHONE for the deprecated channels) set,
# sends one real message:
#     npm run verify:otp
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OTP_SECRET=generate_with_openssl_rand_hex_32
OTP_DELIVERY_CHANNEL=email

# The Resend API key (re_...) and the verified sender the code arrives from.
# The from-domain must be verified in the Resend dashboard (DNS records on
# businesshelper.app) or every send is refused — npm run verify:otp checks it.
RESEND_API_KEY=re_your_resend_api_key
OTP_EMAIL_FROM="Business Helper <firmas@businesshelper.app>"

# --- Deprecated OTP channels (still functional) + outbound WhatsApp ----------
# The payment reminders in lib/whatsappOutbound.ts share these Twilio/Meta
# credentials and fall back to wa.me deep links while they are absent.
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=ACyour_twilio_account_sid
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=your_twilio_auth_token
# Sender for the deprecated sms channel. TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER is the legacy
# name and is still read as a fallback.
TWILIO_SMS_NUMBER=+14155238886
TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER=+14155238886
# Sender for the deprecated whatsapp channel via Twilio. Setting it makes
# Twilio win over Meta below.
TWILIO_WHATSAPP_NUMBER=+14155238886

# whatsapp channel via the Meta Cloud API, used when TWILIO_WHATSAPP_NUMBER is
# unset. META_GRAPH_API_VERSION is optional and defaults to v21.0.
META_WHATSAPP_TOKEN=your_meta_whatsapp_permanent_token
META_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=your_meta_phone_number_id
META_GRAPH_API_VERSION=v21.0

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Gemini AI Operations Assistant (@google/genai)
# Required for natural language receivables query parsing & smart reminders
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GEMINI_API_KEY=AIzaSyYourGeminiAPIKeyHere
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Product Analytics (PostHog — issue #37)
# The core quote-to-cash funnel; ANALYTICS_EVENTS in lib/analytics.ts is the
# live list (signup_started … payment_confirmed, cfdi_issued, …).
# Unset key = analytics is a silent no-op everywhere (demo, local dev, CI).
# The key is a PostHog *project API key* (phc_...), which is public by design —
# hence NEXT_PUBLIC_. Host is OPTIONAL and defaults to https://us.i.posthog.com;
# set the EU ingestion host instead if the project was created in the EU region.
# No PII is ever sent in event properties: lib/analytics.ts strips phones, emails,
# RFC, and names. Note that PostHog *person* properties (set by identify() in
# components/PostHogInit.tsx) do carry email and name.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_your_posthog_project_api_key
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5b. Error Monitoring (Sentry) — OPTIONAL, and the pair to analytics above.
# Analytics tells you where users dropped; this tells you whether it was our
# fault. Unset = nothing transmits and the log says so
# ([MONITOR NOT CONFIGURED — NOTHING TRANSMITTED]); it never fabricates a
# dispatch. Runs on the official @sentry/nextjs SDK — the one exception to the
# raw-REST posture Stripe, Facturapi and Resend follow here, because unhandled
# Server Component and Edge errors never reach a hand-written call site.
# Paste the DSN exactly as Sentry issues it:
#   https://<publicKey>@<org>.ingest.<region>.sentry.io/<projectId>
# SENTRY_DSN is server-side and Edge. NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN is the browser's
# (needed for app/global-error.tsx and Session Replay); a Sentry DSN is public
# by design, but it is write-only — it cannot read your issues. Set both.
# PII is stripped before sending: emails, RFC, CLABE and phone numbers are
# redacted from messages, stack traces, breadcrumbs, logs and extras, while
# organization_id, user_id and route survive so an alert says which tenant and
# which route. Session Replay masks all text, all inputs and all media.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SENTRY_DSN=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=

# Optional overrides. Unset is fine — the environment is derived from VERCEL_ENV
# and the release from the deployed commit SHA.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=production
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_RELEASE=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5c. Sentry source maps — BUILD-TIME ONLY, and only needed for readable stack
# traces in production. Without these the build still succeeds and errors still
# report; the frames just point at minified code.
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN is a SECRET (it can write releases to your org) — set it in
# Vercel's environment variables, or locally in .env.sentry-build-plugin, which
# is gitignored. Create it at https://sentry.io/settings/auth-tokens/ with the
# project:releases and org:read scopes.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SENTRY_ORG=
SENTRY_PROJECT=
SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Application Environment & Media CDN Flags
# Set to 'production' on Vercel deployment with production CDN storage URL
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NODE_ENV=production
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://businesshelper.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_CDN_URL=https://cdn.businesshelper.app
